.TH UNIM-CONFIG 1 "April 2026" "UNIM 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unim\-config \- UNIM configuration manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unim\-config
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unim\-config
reads and writes the UNIM user configuration file
.RB ( ~/.config/unim/config.yaml ).
It is a thin CLI on top of the same configuration backend used by the
.B unim\-gui\-gtk
settings dialog and the daemon itself, and it is the recommended way to
script configuration changes from shell environments.
.PP
Changes take effect immediately for the running daemon via the
.B ConfigChanged
D-Bus signal; no restart is required.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B show
Print the current configuration as YAML to standard output.
.TP
.BR set " \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR"
Set a single configuration key. The
.I KEY
uses dot notation (for example
.BR engine.korean.layout ).
Valid keys and value ranges follow the same schema as the GTK settings
dialog.
.TP
.B path
Print the absolute path of the active configuration file.
.TP
.B reset
Reset the configuration file to default values. Asks for confirmation.
.TP
.B interactive
Launch an interactive prompt-driven configuration session. Useful when a
graphical settings dialog is not available.
.TP
.BR help " [\fICOMMAND\fR]"
Print help text for the program or for a specific subcommand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print top-level help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/config.yaml
The configuration file managed by this tool.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unim (1),
.BR unim\-cli (1),
.BR unim\-gui\-gtk (1)
